From: Claude <claude@assistant.local>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 06:31:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add voxel chunks with face-culled meshing + Perlin noise
 terrain

- settings.py: fixed mouse sensitivity (was 60x too low) and player speed
  (was too fast), added world-generation tuning constants
- world_generator.py: Perlin noise heightmap (pnoise2) per (x,z) column
- chunk.py: 16x16x16 voxel grid per chunk, builds mesh from ONLY the faces
  touching air (huge triangle-count savings), grass/dirt/stone layering
- chunk_manager.py: builds a RENDER_DISTANCE grid of chunks, positions each
  with its own model-matrix translation at render time
- app.py: swapped the single test Cube for the full ChunkManager-driven
  world, repositioned camera to spawn above the generated terrain
